summary:
- topic: Student Recognition
  text: The board began the meeting by recognizing the South Portland High School
    marching band, who won a gold medal and a five-star rating at the Maine Band Directors
    Association state finals.
- topic: Contracts
  text: The board unanimously ratified the FY2025-2028 collective bargaining agreement
    with the South Portland Teachers Association (SPTA).
- topic: Contracts
  text: During public comment, teachers and union leaders thanked the board for the
    SPTA contract and urged a swift resolution for the ongoing negotiations with the
    South Portland Education Support Professionals Association (SPESPA).
- topic: FY2026 Budget
  text: The Finance Director presented a budget update, noting a projected $337,000
    deficit for the current fiscal year (FY2026) would be offset by a one-time $815,000
    geothermal tax credit. She warned that the district's fund balance is nearing
    depletion, which will create significant challenges for the FY2027 budget.
- topic: Facilities
  text: The Director of Operations reported on significant soil and turf issues at
    the South Portland Middle School field, outlining a multi-step remediation plan.
    The board discussed holding the original contractor financially responsible for
    the necessary repairs.
- topic: Policy
  text: The board approved the second and final reading of Policy JJIF, concerning
    the management of concussions and other head injuries.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The superintendent announced the resignation of Gretchen McCloy, Director
    of Community Partnerships. Board members expressed their gratitude for her service
    and significant contributions to the district.
- topic: Board Business
  text: As it was the last regular meeting for Chair Ratliff and Member Rocher, the
    board shared farewell remarks and thanked them for their service.
